# C# file size limits

Grid Dungeon targets **modular agent context** (~32k tokens ≈ **2,100 lines** of dense C#). Monolithic files block review, search, and local inference slices.

**Epic:** [griddungeon-game #341](https://github.com/miramocha/griddungeon-game/issues/341)

## Caps (`Assets/Scripts/**/*.cs`)

| Threshold | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| **≤300 lines** | Default target for new types |
| **301–400 lines** | OK if single responsibility; do not add unrelated features |
| **401–500 lines** | **Stop and split** before landing new behavior — extract helper, presenter, or `partial` |
| **>500 lines** | **Forbidden** for new/edited first-party code except documented Editor exception below |
| **>800 lines** | **Forbidden** everywhere — split required before merge |

**Editor tools** (`Assets/Scripts/Editor/**`): soft cap **800 lines**; still split by panel/tool domain when practical.

**Tests** (`Assets/Tests/**`): prefer **≤400 lines** per fixture; extract shared builders to `GridDungeon.TestShared`.

## Agent / PR rules

1. **Do not create** a new `.cs` file expected to exceed **300 lines** — sketch seams first (shell vs presenter vs coordinator).
2. **Do not append** large features to a file already **>400 lines** — extract first, then implement.
3. **No `#region` as a split substitute** — extract a real type or `partial` file ([`unity-csharp-formatting`](unity-csharp-formatting.mdc)).
4. **Prefer existing homes** — presenters under `UI/Views/`, simulators in `Core/`, phase logic in `*PhaseController`, Editor panels beside domain folder.
5. **Touching a legacy god file** — budget a split in the same PR or file a child of #341; do not grow line count without team intent.

## Split patterns (prefer in order)

| Pattern | When |
|---------|------|
| **Extract presenter / coordinator** | `MonoBehaviour` mixes bind, input, and layout |
| **`partial class`** | One public type, `{TypeName}.{Concern}.cs` — see [class naming patterns § Partial class file naming](https://github.com/miramocha/griddungeon-design-docs/blob/main/docs/04-dev/class-naming-patterns.md#partial-class-file-naming-locked) |
| **Static helper** | Pure formatting, catalog build, focus rules |
| **Interface + host** | Cross-phase contracts (`ICombatSkillPickerHost`, `IPartyFormationKeyboardView`) |

Respect asmdef boundaries — `Core` never references `Runtime` or `UI` ([`unity-core-campaign-assembly`](unity-core-campaign-assembly.mdc)).

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — 200 lines added to HubHudView for hospital picker
// ✅ GOOD — HubHospitalCharacterPicker + thin bind in HubHudView
```

## Review smell

File name contains **And** duties (`OverlayView` doing menu + bag + formation + hints) → split before next ticket.
